SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-Sipral-Commercial
Copyright (c) 2026 Sytek

Vanilla's own event_socket.conf.xml listens on "::", which mod_event_socket
cannot bind on this lab's network: the container gets no non-loopback IPv6
address from Docker's own bridge, and vanilla's "::" is not the loopback
alone, it is every address on the box, which is why the log is not "bind
failed", it is "Cannot get information about IP address ::". The socket
never opens, which is also why the image's own healthcheck.sh (fs_cli -x
status, over this socket) always finds it down and the container never goes
healthy. Nothing in this lab reads events over this socket, since the
flows are proven by their own SIP and RTP, so the vanilla default of
listening on every address is not needed either; this file only narrows it
to the address that actually binds.

The path is the same one vanilla's own file lives at, not a new name: this
file has to replace it, not add to it, since mod_event_socket loads exactly
one config by that name rather than including a directory by glob.
-->
<configuration name="event_socket.conf" description="Socket Client">
  <settings>
    <param name="nat-map" value="false"/>
    <param name="listen-ip" value="127.0.0.1"/>
    <param name="listen-port" value="8021"/>
    <param name="password" value="ClueCon"/>
  </settings>
</configuration>
